# Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Base URL of the backend API Gateway (healthcare-ecosystem's apps/gateway).
# Local gateway: http://localhost:3000
# Deployed (Render free tier — cold starts after idle, can take 30-60s):
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://healthcare-app-vtwa.onrender.com

# KNOWN ISSUE (confirmed via browser testing): the deployed backend's CORS
# config does not allow a localhost origin — any browser request to it from
# `pnpm dev`/`pnpm start` running locally is blocked at the CORS preflight,
# even though the exact same request works fine from curl/Node (no CORS
# there — it's a browser-only restriction). A Vite dev-server proxy was
# tried and does NOT work here: TanStack Start's own dev middleware claims
# every request path before Vite's `server.proxy` ever sees it.
#
# To actually exercise login/API calls against the deployed backend from a
# browser, someone with access to the Render deployment needs to add the
# relevant origin(s) (e.g. http://localhost:5173, http://localhost:4173) to
# the gateway's CORS_ORIGINS env var. Until then, point VITE_API_BASE_URL at
# a locally-run backend instead for full browser testing.
